      "spam": false,
      "value": "Hey MatSix, I believe you are confused here... xD First, whitelist is ONLY for avatars. There is no restrictions on Unity or VRC supported asset components for worlds. Only custom scripts are not allowed. Second, what you actually would need, is VRChat to implement the entire asset you are using, to be a part of the VRChat API standard, much the same way VRChat implemented full support for Dynamic Bone asset. This makes this request a much huger request, as adding an asset to VRC is a tall order, one which is rarely ever fulfilled for various reasons, including the fact that every asset you add, is a potential for VRC to need to debug it when things go wrong, or the risk when the asset is no longer supported, having all the old content that relied on it breaking, etc. For this reason it is really rare that VRC will add assets with custom scripts as part of the standard game. Usually only Unity made scripts such as the Post Process stack have a higher chance of being added to the core API.\n\nI know this isn't what you want to hear... trust me, if VRC would add random asset requests, the community has TONS of amazing assets (that require the custom scripts added to the core game) that would be great additions. This is actually a topic of debate we had back about 2-3 years ago with some of the veterans and the devs, it's something that would be really nice, but also has too many drawbacks atm. \n\nBy the way, a potential work around is to model your terrain as an actual mesh, instead of a Unity terrain object, then you can put a standard shader on the mesh instead, giving you access to all those features you just mentioned. Of course a terrain will use a splatmap... for that you'd need a custom shader which can get pretty advanced... But there are options.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
